# API Design Skill

Reference with **@claude-skills/api-design** when designing or reviewing APIs.

## When to use

- User asks to design or review REST/HTTP APIs, request/response shape, or versioning
- Defining endpoints, status codes, errors, and contracts
- Aligning with OpenAPI/Swagger or project API conventions

## Principles

- Use standard HTTP methods and status codes; 422 for validation, 404 for missing resource, etc.
- Consistent error shape (e.g. code, message, details); use ValidationResult.raise_if_invalid() where applicable
- Version via URL path or header per project; avoid breaking changes without versioning
- Document endpoints, params, and responses; keep OpenAPI in sync if used
- Consider pagination, filtering, and rate limiting for list and heavy endpoints
